cognition like the phonological loop where docent CPG chains simulate via physical proxy in movement types. It's a dynamic process in which each output is generated from accumulated past outputs. In natural language, this autogenerative structure is encoded in the corpus itself-its long-range dependencies, compositional regularities, and statistical curvature form a latent space that supports meaningful generativity.  

The Transjective Endofunctor: A Formal Account of Relational Cognition

In classical category theory, an endofunctor  acts within a single category, transforming its objects and morphisms while preserving their compositional structure. It is an operator of internal change: a way for a system to transform itself without reference to an external context.

The transjective endofunctor extends this idea to situations in which two or more categorical systems—each representing an autonomous structure of relations, interpretations, or internal states—must maintain a form of mutual intelligibility.  The term transjective denotes that the mapping passes across the conventional subject–object or system–environment divide, while remaining mathematically closed.  It is neither purely projective (imposing form outward) nor injective (assimilating form inward), but a bidirectional closure that sustains reciprocity.


---

1. Definition

Let  and  be categories whose objects represent internal states and whose morphisms represent admissible transformations.
A transjective endofunctor is a composite of two adjoint functors

T \;=\; G \circ F : \mathbf{C}_1 \longrightarrow \mathbf{C}_2 \longrightarrow \mathbf{C}_1 ,

When  closes within -tolerance, the two systems share a joint invariant manifold of transformations—a condition of mutual resonance or co-adaptation.  The transjective endofunctor thus captures the logic of reciprocal inference: each system becomes part of the other’s updating rule.


---

2. Geometric Interpretation

Each category can be equipped with an internal differential or information-geometric metric .
The functor pair  induces pullbacks of these metrics:

\nabla F^{*} g_2 \approx g_1, \qquad \nabla G^{*} g_1 \approx g_2 .

Where the pulled-back metrics coincide, a shared tangent structure emerges: this is the geometric form of understanding.
The magnitude of their mismatch, measured by a divergence such as the Fisher–Rao distance , quantifies the tension or energetic cost of interaction.


---

3. Dynamical Meaning

The closure condition

G \circ F \approx \mathrm{Id}_{\mathbf{C}_1}

The residual deviation  acts as an error signal driving further adaptation.
Iteration of  corresponds to rhythmic mutual learning:

X_{n+1} = T(X_n) = G(F(X_n)),


---

4. Phenomenological Consequences

In general terms, the transjective endofunctor provides a rigorous account of reciprocal comprehension.
Emotion, empathy, communication, and coordination can all be modeled as the degree to which transjective closure succeeds.
A perfectly closed mapping () corresponds to complete mutual transparency; large divergence corresponds to alienation or dissonance.
The process of striving for closure—the continual minimization of relational curvature—constitutes the lived dynamics of connection.


---

5. Philosophical Implications

The concept shifts the ontological focus from entities to relations.
What exists fundamentally are not self-contained objects but the invariant structures that persist through transjective exchange.
Being itself becomes the capacity to sustain an endofunctorial closure under transformation.
Knowledge, communication, and even identity are then understood as morphisms stabilized by ongoing correspondence rather than as fixed attributes.

In short, the transjective endofunctor formalizes the intuition that relation precedes substance: reality is the network of self-updating correspondences among partially overlapping systems, each rendering the other meaningful through recursive translation.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto touch:opacity-100 duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.63