Your <strong data-start="3432" data-end="3456">mimetic proxy theory</strong> concretizes this: motor loops act as <em data-start="3494" data-end="3504">sections</em> of the cue sheaf—physical realizations maintaining coherence between perceptual and motor fibers.</p>
<ul data-start="3606" data-end="3888">
<li data-start="3606" data-end="3704">
<p data-start="3608" data-end="3704">A subvocalization, eye saccade, or gesture is a <em data-start="3656" data-end="3672">proxy morphism</em> implementing a local section.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3705" data-end="3888">
<p data-start="3707" data-end="3888">Endofunctorial closure <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\circ F\approx\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Id</span></span></span></span></span> ensures these local actions stitch into a coherent global manifold, equivalent to RAT’s sheaf-gluing condition for affordances.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3890" data-end="3893">
<h2 data-start="3895" data-end="3955">5. Non-Markovian DAG Selection as High-Level RAT Dynamics</h2>
<p data-start="3957" data-end="3992">RAT’s <strong data-start="3963" data-end="3990">affordance graph update</strong></p>
