<li data-start="5573" data-end="5744">
<p data-start="5576" data-end="5744"><strong data-start="5576" data-end="5598">Cognitive Economy:</strong><br data-start="5598" data-end="5601">
Relegation conserves thermodynamic work <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>R</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W = \int |\nabla R|^2 dt</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1202em; vertical-align: -0.3061em;"></span><span class="mop op-symbol small-op" style="margin-right: 0.19445em; position: relative; top: -0.0006em;">∫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∣∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span>, aligning with the Free Energy Principle’s drive toward minimal action.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5746" data-end="5984">
<p data-start="5749" data-end="5984"><strong data-start="5749" data-end="5782">Forgetting and De-relegation:</strong><br data-start="5782" data-end="5785">
If relevance curvature is reintroduced (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>R</mi><mo mathvariant="normal">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla R \neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span>) due to environmental novelty, the endofunctor reopens: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span> reverts from idempotent to adaptive, re-engaging transjective inference.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="5986" data-end="5989">
<h2 data-start="5991" data-end="6021">5. Theoretical Implications</h2>
<h3 data-start="6023" data-end="6065">5.1 Entropic and Geometric Convergence</h3>
<p data-start="6066" data-end="6320">Aspect Relegation unifies <em data-start="6092" data-end="6113">energy minimization</em> (RAT) and <em data-start="6124" data-end="6142">metric alignment</em> (ATT) as a single convergence process.<br data-start="6181" data-end="6184">
It describes cognition’s descent along an entropic manifold toward <em data-start="6251" data-end="6278">relevance-free attractors</em>, where representation becomes procedural.</p>
<h3 data-start="6322" data-end="6363">5.2 Category-Theoretic Generalization</h3>
<p data-start="6364" data-end="6411">Formally, <strong data-start="6374" data-end="6395">Aspect Relegation</strong> corresponds to:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Find&nbsp;</mtext><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>&nbsp;such&nbsp;that&nbsp;</mtext><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∃</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi><mtext>&nbsp;with&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Find } T: \mathbf{C}_1 \to \mathbf{C}_1 \text{ such that } T^2 = T, \quad \text{and } \exists \, R : X \to \mathbb{R} \text{ with } \nabla R = 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Find&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8361em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0141em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;such&nbsp;that&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8641em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">and&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord">∃</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;with&nbsp;</span></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6570" data-end="6678">This is an <strong data-start="6581" data-end="6622">idempotent, energy-stable endofunctor</strong>, representing a permanently relegated cognitive aspect.</p>
<h3 data-start="6680" data-end="6722">5.3 Neurocomputational and AI Parallel</h3>
<p data-start="6723" data-end="6889">In artificial agents modeled under RAT’s cue-relevance architectures, ART predicts that stable affordance graphs <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.22222em;">V</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> emerge when affordance weights converge:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi mathvariant="normal">∀</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dw_{ij}}{dt} = 0, \quad \forall (i,j) \in E,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.0574em; vertical-align: -0.686em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3714em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.686em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∀</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6947" data-end="7053">mirroring the biological flattening of relevance curvature and functional autonomy of procedural circuits.</p>
<hr data-start="7055" data-end="7058">
<h2 data-start="7060" data-end="7076">6. Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start="7078" data-end="7615"><strong data-start="7078" data-end="7112">Aspect Relegation Theory (ART)</strong> describes the <em data-start="7127" data-end="7176">thermodynamic and categorical limit of learning</em>—the point where reciprocal inference loops achieve stable identity and relevance gradients vanish.<br data-start="7275" data-end="7278">
Through the RAT framework, this appears as gradient quenching; through the ATT framework, as idempotent transjective closure.<br data-start="7403" data-end="7406">
In both, cognition evolves toward entropic equilibrium, delegating formerly conscious aspects into invariant morphic circuits—a geometric and energetic definition of <em data-start="7572" data-end="7615">automaticity as transjective equilibrium.</em></p>
