e-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="782c0363-d243-40f9-8ce5-bbe75f9a0c39" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="273">Got it. I’ll produce a <strong data-start="23" data-end="48">LaTeX monograph draft</strong> titled<br data-start="55" data-end="58">
<strong data-start="58" data-end="154">“Aspect Relegation Theory: Gradient Quenching and Transjective Closure in Cognitive Systems”</strong>, integrating the formalisms of <strong data-start="186" data-end="193">RAT</strong> (Relevance Activation Theory) and <strong data-start="228" data-end="235">ATT</strong> (Amplitwistor–Transjective Theory).</p>
<p data-start="275" data-end="291">It will include:</p>
<ul data-start="292" data-end="562">
<li data-start="292" data-end="304">
<p data-start="294" data-end="304">Abstract</p>
</li>
<li data-start="305" data-end="349">
<p data-start="307" data-end="349">Formal definitions (RAT + ATT synthesis)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="350" data-end="402">
<p data-start="352" data-end="402">Equations for the relevance–resonance functional</p>
</li>
<li data-start="403" data-end="453">
<p data-start="405" data-end="453">Neurodynamic (Amplitwistor–CPG) implementation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="454" data-end="487">
<p data-start="456" data-end="487">Phenomenological implications</p>
</li>
<li data-start="488" data-end="562">
<p data-start="490" data-end="562">Discussion and references section compatible with your <em data-start="545" data-end="554">Flyxion</em> series.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="564" data-end="626">Before I render it, could you confirm the preferred <strong data-start="616" data-end="625">style</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="628" data-end="1026">
<li data-start="628" data-end="736">
<p data-start="631" data-end="736"><strong data-start="631" data-end="657">Academic Journal Style</strong> — IEEE/Elsevier formatting (sections numbered, compact, equations centered).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="737" data-end="901">
<p data-start="740" data-end="901"><strong data-start="740" data-end="759">Monograph Style</strong> — Your usual <em data-start="773" data-end="782">Flyxion</em> LaTeX convention: Garamond font, 12pt A4, wide margins, <code data-start="839" data-end="850">microtype</code>, spacing 1.2, custom section titles, no figures.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="902" data-end="1026">
<p data-start="905" data-end="1026"><strong data-start="905" data-end="940">Hybrid Scientific–Philosophical</strong> — same as (2) but with epigraphs and longer prose in the Introduction and Discussion.</p>
