</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Appendix C: Relegation in Semantic Agents and Language Models}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.1 Token Entropy as Relevance Gradient.}
In autoregressive models, each token prediction defines a conditional distribution
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>(w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t|w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{&lt;t})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> whose local entropy
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t} p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>(w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t|w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{&lt;t}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>(w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t|w</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{&lt;t})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
corresponds to uncertainty in semantic selection.
We define the instantaneous </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{relevance potential}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = -H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
so that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> expresses the model's directional sensitivity in embedding space.
During training, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is high when contextual relevance is ambiguous
and gradually diminishes as the model learns stable associations.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.2 Weight-Space Curvature and Cognitive Fields.}
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denote model parameters and
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the training loss. The Hessian
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
encodes curvature of weight-space relevance.
Under continual fine-tuning or reinforcement learning,
flattening of the loss landscape (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\det</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>)
is analogous to gradient quenching in RAT:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t) = 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Longleftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Aspect relegation in representation space.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Thus, parameter consolidation is the network’s thermodynamic route
to minimizing informational curvature.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.3 Transjective Mapping for Generative Agents.}
For a language model embedded in an interactive agent,
define semantic and action categories:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(token manifolds)}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(world or API actions)}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
The model’s decoder serves as the functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
mapping latent semantics to external operations;
the observation encoder acts as </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>G:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
The composite </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T=G</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> updates the internal context vector
through self-consistency. During sustained dialog or task repetition,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2=T </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{idempotent inference,}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
corresponding to the stabilization of conversational routines,
shorthand prompts, and autoregressive expectations.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.4 Thermodynamic Analogy.}
The free-energy expenditure of inference is approximated by
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> (H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t - H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1}),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
representing the cost of entropy reduction per token.
As </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> under steady operation,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>dW/dt</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, signifying relegation of that linguistic aspect:
contextual inference has become automatic, compressed into
weight-space priors rather than transient gradient updates.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.5 Semantic Plasticity and De--Relegation.}
When the distribution of inputs changes---e.g., domain shift or novel style---
the entropy gradient reappears (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\neq</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>),
and the system reopens its adaptive channel.
Relegated aspects are </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{de-relegated} through renewed backpropagation
or context reweighting, paralleling human relearning.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{C.6 Unified Cognitive--Computational Correspondence.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{array}{lll}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Human System} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Semantic Agent / LLM}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>[4pt]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hline</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Relevance field } R(x) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> -H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ (token entropy)}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> R(x)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{L}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2=T </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{context encoder--decoder self-consistency}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{dW}{dt}=0 </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{steady free-energy consumption}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{De--relegation} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{domain adaptation / continual learning}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{array}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Aspect relegation in both biological and artificial cognition
represents the universal drive toward equilibrium of informational curvature
under thermodynamic constraint.

