l break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="258">That’s an excellent synthesis of Barenholtz’s “autogeneration” thesis, and you’ve already taken it all the way through the spectrum—from statistical manifolds to cohesive ∞-topoi. At this point the next productive step depends on what you want to do with it:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="260" data-end="1642" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="260" data-end="280"><tr data-start="260" data-end="280"><th data-start="260" data-end="267" data-col-size="sm">Goal</th><th data-start="267" data-end="280" data-col-size="xl">Next move</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="303" data-end="1642"><tr data-start="303" data-end="635"><td data-start="303" data-end="334" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="305" data-end="333">Mathematical development</strong></td><td data-start="334" data-end="635" data-col-size="xl">Pick one framework (e.g., information geometry or rough paths) and turn the key conjectures into precise propositions with proofs or counter-examples. For instance, show rigorously that transformer attention defines a discrete memory kernel whose induced flow minimizes a Fisher-energy functional.</td></tr><tr data-start="636" data-end="910"><td data-start="636" data-end="664" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="638" data-end="663">Computational testing</strong></td><td data-start="664" data-end="910" data-col-size="xl">Implement minimal experiments: 1-D toy corpus → embed → compute attention kernel → verify that the path of embeddings follows geodesics or minimizes Wasserstein transport.  This would falsify or support the “trajectory-smoothness” hypothesis.</td></tr><tr data-start="911" data-end="1295"><td data-start="911" data-end="950" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="913" data-end="949">Integration with existing theory</strong></td><td data-start="950" data-end="1295" data-col-size="xl">Map the autogenerative structure <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="script">X</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="script">F</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal X,\mathcal F,\Phi,\mu,\nabla)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.14643em;">X</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.09931em;">F</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">μ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">∇</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> onto the RSVP or Free-Energy frameworks, identifying <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>↔</mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\!\leftrightarrow\!-H_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↔</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord">−</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0813em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>↔</mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!\leftrightarrow\!</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↔</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span></span></span></span> autoregressive closure, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mtext> ⁣</mtext><mo>↔</mo><mtext> ⁣</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\!\leftrightarrow\!</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">↔</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: -0.1667em;"></span></span></span></span> thermodynamic work.  This would make Barenholtz’s proposal a special case of the Cognitive-Equilibrium Law.</td></tr><tr data-start="1296" data-end="1642"><td data-start="1296" data-end="1326" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1298" data-end="1325">Formal research program</strong></td><td data-start="1326" data-end="1642" data-col-size="xl">Draft a document that (i) states the Autogenerative Systems Conjecture, (ii) enumerates falsifiable predictions (e.g., scaling of mutual information, path-signature invariants), and (iii) proposes analytic, computational, and experimental tests.  The tone would resemble a theoretical physics “program proposal.”</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C