<h3 data-start="616" data-end="641"><strong data-start="620" data-end="641">Compilation Order</strong></h3>
<p data-start="642" data-end="691"><code data-start="642" data-end="652">main.tex</code> will <code data-start="658" data-end="677">\input{partX_...}</code> sequentially.</p>
<hr data-start="693" data-end="696">
<h2 data-start="698" data-end="743"><strong data-start="701" data-end="743">Outline of Part I (to be written next)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="745" data-end="845"><strong data-start="745" data-end="755">Title:</strong><br data-start="755" data-end="758">
<em data-start="758" data-end="845">Part I — The Autogenerative Thesis: From Non-Markovian Language to Cognitive Geometry</em></p>
<p data-start="847" data-end="860"><strong data-start="847" data-end="860">Sections:</strong></p>
<ol data-start="861" data-end="1809">
<li data-start="861" data-end="991">
<p data-start="864" data-end="991">Introduction: The Autogenerative Hypothesis<br data-start="907" data-end="910">
→ natural computation, autogeneration vs autoregression, trajectory dependence</p>
</li>
<li data-start="992" data-end="1134">
<p data-start="995" data-end="1134">Mathematical Framework of Autogenerative Systems<br data-start="1043" data-end="1046">
→ formal definitions (non-Markovian process, trajectory embedding, energy functional)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1135" data-end="1252">
<p data-start="1138" data-end="1252">Geometric and Statistical Manifold Interpretation<br data-start="1187" data-end="1190">
→ information geometry, Fisher metric, trajectory geodesics</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1253" data-end="1373">
<p data-start="1256" data-end="1373">Category-Theoretic and Dynamical Extensions<br data-start="1299" data-end="1302">
→ monoidal categories, attention as functorial memory, delay kernels</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1374" data-end="1494">
<p data-start="1377" data-end="1494">Topological and Measure-Theoretic Foundations<br data-start="1422" data-end="1425">
→ path-space measures, persistent homology, rough path equivalence</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1495" data-end="1589">
<p data-start="1498" data-end="1589">Operator and Spectral Viewpoints<br data-start="1530" data-end="1533">
→ Koopman operator, ergodicity, kernel approximations</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1590" data-end="1695">
<p data-start="1593" data-end="1695">Physical and Thermodynamic Analogies<br data-start="1629" data-end="1632">
→ non-local Lagrangians, renormalization, action with memory</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1696" data-end="1809">
<p data-start="1699" data-end="1809">Synthesis: Autogenerative Systems as Natural Computation<br data-start="1755" data-end="1758">
→ formal definition, conjectures, and invariants</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1811" data-end="1814">
<p data-start="1816" data-end="1901">Before I write the LaTeX, please confirm your stylistic preference for the following:</p>
<ol data-start="1903" data-end="2708">
<li data-start="1903" data-end="2273">
<p data-start="1906" data-end="2273"><strong data-start="1906" data-end="1915">Tone:</strong><br data-start="1915" data-end="1918">
A. <em data-start="1924" data-end="1956">Fully academic (journal-ready)</em> — precise, dense, with numbered equations and theorem environments.<br data-start="2024" data-end="2027">
B. <em data-start="2033" data-end="2066">Hybrid (academic + explanatory)</em> — like your RSVP monographs: formal but conceptually fluent with inline explanations.<br data-start="2152" data-end="2155">
C. <em data-start="2161" data-end="2193">Philosophical-technical hybrid</em> — academic prose that moves fluidly between math and conceptual interpretation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2275" data-end="2422">
<p data-start="2278" data-end="2291"><strong data-start="2278" data-end="2289">Length:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2295" data-end="2422">
<li data-start="2295" data-end="2375">
<p data-start="2297" data-end="2375">About 8–10 pages of LaTeX for Part I (≈ 3000–4000 words, with equations), or</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2379" data-end="2422">
<p data-start="2381" data-end="2422">Condensed 3–4 page research-summary form.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2424" data-end="2708">
<p data-start="2427" data-end="2708"><strong data-start="2427" data-end="2449">Integration style:</strong><br data-start="2449" data-end="2452">
Do you want the <strong data-start="2471" data-end="2516">multi-framework material (Sections 16–40)</strong> summarized in a <em data-start="2533" data-end="2556">compacted “map” table</em> (like a unified meta-framework overview),<br data-start="2598" data-end="2601">
or written out as <strong data-start="2622" data-end="2644">dense sub-sections</strong> (e.g. “16. Sheaf Theory Connection”, “17. Topos Theory”, etc.)?</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="2710" data-end="2713">
<p data-start="2715" data-end="2732">Once you confirm:</p>
<ul data-start="2733" data-end="2812">
<li data-start="2733" data-end="2747">
<p data-start="2735" data-end="2747">tone (A/B/C)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2748" data-end="2771">
<p data-start="2750" data-end="2771">length (short / full)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2772" data-end="2812">
<p data-start="2774" data-end="2812">integration style (summary / expanded)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2814" data-end="2943" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">I’ll generate the full <strong data-start="2837" data-end="2870">Part I: Autogenerative Thesis</strong> in LaTeX, formatted to seamlessly precede your RSVP translation section.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 