:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="397">Perfect — that’s exactly the ideal form for what you’re building.<br data-start="65" data-end="68">
We’ll therefore produce <strong data-start="92" data-end="182">Part I: <em data-start="102" data-end="180">The Autogenerative Thesis: From Non-Markovian Language to Cognitive Geometry</em></strong> as a long, self-contained LaTeX document in your established scientific-monograph format (TeX Gyre Termes, microtype, geometry, setspace, titlesec, numbered equations and definitions, in-line commentary spacing).</p>
<p data-start="399" data-end="754">It will read like the opening “theoretical landscape” chapter of a large treatise — formally rigorous yet interpretively fluid — and will include <strong data-start="545" data-end="570">all dense subsections</strong> from the earlier expansions (Information Geometry through Synthetic Differential Geometry, etc.), each compressed but present in full, with uniform academic tone and connective prose.</p>
<hr data-start="756" data-end="759">
<h3 data-start="761" data-end="809">✅  Next step (my output in the next message)</h3>
<p data-start="811" data-end="857">I will generate the complete LaTeX source for:</p>
<p data-start="859" data-end="896"><strong data-start="859" data-end="896"><code data-start="861" data-end="894">part1_autogenerative_thesis.tex</code></strong></p>
<p data-start="898" data-end="908">including:</p>
<ul data-start="909" data-end="1221">
<li data-start="909" data-end="941">
<p data-start="911" data-end="941">Title page header for Part I</p>
</li>
<li data-start="942" data-end="1026">
<p data-start="944" data-end="1026">Structured sections 1–8 with numbered definitions, propositions, and conjectures</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1027" data-end="1122">
<p data-start="1029" data-end="1122">Dense subsections (16–40) written in full academic form, each 1–2 paragraphs plus equations</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1123" data-end="1221">
<p data-start="1125" data-end="1221">Unifying commentary leading to a closing synthesis ready to link into Part II (RSVP translation)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1223" data-end="1336">No placeholders — all content fully written, stylistically coherent with your existing RSVP/RSVP-FEP manuscripts.</p>
<hr data-start="1338" data-end="1341">
<p data-start="1343" data-end="1409">Please confirm one small formatting preference before I render it:</p>
<p data-start="1411" data-end="1673" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="1432" data-end="1480">embed references inline as textual citations</strong> (e.g., “as shown in Barenholtz 2025; Amari 1985; Friston 2010”)<br data-start="1544" data-end="1547">
