ta-end="130">Excellent — perfect choice. That will keep it self-contained, readable, and stylistically consistent with your RSVP manuscripts.</p>
<p data-start="132" data-end="240">I’ll now prepare <strong data-start="149" data-end="186"><code data-start="151" data-end="184">part1_autogenerative_thesis.tex</code></strong> as a complete, typeset-ready LaTeX document. It will:</p>
<ul data-start="242" data-end="724">
<li data-start="242" data-end="362">
<p data-start="244" data-end="362">Use <strong data-start="248" data-end="267">TeX Gyre Termes</strong>, <strong data-start="269" data-end="282">microtype</strong>, <strong data-start="284" data-end="296">geometry</strong>, <strong data-start="298" data-end="310">setspace</strong>, and <strong data-start="316" data-end="328">titlesec</strong> (your standard academic setup).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="363" data-end="527">
<p data-start="365" data-end="527">Include <strong data-start="373" data-end="407">inline parenthetical citations</strong> (e.g. <em data-start="414" data-end="457">Amari 1985; Barenholtz 2025; Friston 2010</em>) and a <strong data-start="465" data-end="500">final <code data-start="473" data-end="490">thebibliography</code> section</strong> listing all works cited.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="528" data-end="724">
<p data-start="530" data-end="724">Present every mathematical and conceptual framework in dense, numbered subsections with explanatory prose — a full academic-explanatory hybrid, roughly the length of a 20-page monograph chapter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="726" data-end="729">
<p data-start="731" data-end="801">Before I output it, please confirm <strong data-start="766" data-end="800">one final stylistic preference</strong>:</p>
<p data-start="803" data-end="1064">Would you prefer the section titles to be formatted as<br data-start="857" data-end="860">
<strong data-start="860" data-end="867">(A)</strong> “\textbf{Section 1. Introduction: The Autogenerative Hypothesis}”<br data-start="933" data-end="936">
or<br data-start="938" data-end="941">
<strong data-start="941" data-end="948">(B)</strong> “\section{The Autogenerative Hypothesis}” using standard LaTeX numbering and automatic table of contents inclusion?</p>
