The categorical semantics lifts naturally to delay systems. Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be a continuous-time embedding and define a state-dependent memory kernel </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> derived from attention over the past. Then
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{dh}{dt}(t)=F</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>(h(t),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>t K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>G</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>(h(t-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
is a Volterra-type equation with content-defined delay. The kernel </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the continuous analogue of attention weights </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ti}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (Barenholtz 2025).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Existence and Attractor of Closure]
Assume </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is locally Lipschitz and the memory kernel satisfies </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>&lt;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> uniformly in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, with a strict contraction on average. Then the flow admits a unique compact global attractor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; if </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the time-</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> stroboscopic map of this flow, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is idempotent on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and equals the transjective closure on its basin.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Idea]
Volterra equations with integrable kernels generate asymptotically compact semigroups. A contraction-on-average yields a unique global attractor. The stroboscopic map </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> inherits compactness and projects onto the attractor, hence </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2=T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Amplitwistor Networks and Phase Condensation}

Represent cortical oscillations as amplitwistor triples </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(Z,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tilde</span></span><span> Z,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{amp}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be their manifold. The semantic functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> selects a CPG mode whose oscillatory phase aligns with a semantic direction, and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>G</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> pulls phase-locked dynamics back to semantics. Relegation corresponds to phase condensation:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{d}{dt}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\arg</span></span><span>(Z</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tilde</span></span><span> Z)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dim</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{active}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\downarrow</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
reducing information curvature and collapsing the adjunction misfit.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Summary of Section 4.}
Autogeneration admits a tight categorical–dynamical formulation: contexts form a monoidal category, autoregression is a natural transformation, and cognition’s embodiment loop is an adjunction whose composite </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> closes idempotently at equilibrium. Aspect relegation is precisely this </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-closure, equivalent to vanishing relevance gradient and zero epistemic work (Amari 1985; Friston 2010; Barenholtz 2025).
