</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Predictive Filtration Stability]
We say an autogenerative system has </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{stable filtration} if for any </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> there exists </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that for all </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t &gt; T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{E}[h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t] - h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span> &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

This expresses that predictive geometry converges on a self-consistent manifold as context accrues.  
In linguistic terms: beyond sufficient context, the internal curvature of prediction stabilizes.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proposition}[Trajectory-Dependent Predictability]
Stable filtration is equivalent to the existence of a path-dependent embedding </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{0:t})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{0:t}),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{and}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} - h</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = o(1),
