</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Measure-Theoretic Non-Markovianity and Tail Dependence}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>I(X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1};X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:t})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denote mutual information.  
Autogenerative systems satisfy power-law tail dependence:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
I(X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1}; X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:t-k} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t-k+1:t}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sim</span></span><span> k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> 0&lt;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>&lt;1.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
By contrast, Markov processes exhibit exponential decay </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span> k}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
This polynomial tail is a hallmark of non-Markovian computation (Bak 1996).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Irreducible Long Memory]
A process has irreducible long memory if no truncation window </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>k &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> yields
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
I(X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1}; X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{1:t-k} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t-k+1:t}) &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
for arbitrarily small </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
