</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Autogenerative Tail Law]
Autogenerative sequence manifolds obey polynomial-decay mutual information scaling.  
In particular, irreducible long memory implies </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{no finite sufficient statistic of fixed dimension exists}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}[Sketch]
If a fixed-length statistic were sufficient, exponential decay would hold by classical Markov compression theorems.  
Polynomial tails violate that bound.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

