w-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="304">Excellent — here’s a <strong data-start="21" data-end="52">complete structural outline</strong> of the paper as we’ve developed it so far, organized into the <strong data-start="115" data-end="135">three main parts</strong> you defined, with all current sections, their content summaries, and indicators for what has already been fully written versus what remains to be written or expanded.</p>
<hr data-start="306" data-end="309">
<h1 data-start="311" data-end="382">🧭 <strong data-start="316" data-end="382">Outline: <em data-start="327" data-end="380">Autogenerative Systems and Aspect Relegation Theory</em></strong></h1>
<h2 data-start="384" data-end="405">Prefatory Material</h2>
<ul data-start="406" data-end="634">
<li data-start="406" data-end="460">
<p data-start="408" data-end="460"><strong data-start="408" data-end="420">Abstract</strong> — Concise summary (to be written last).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="461" data-end="634">
<p data-start="463" data-end="634"><strong data-start="463" data-end="475">Keywords</strong> — <em data-start="478" data-end="634">Autogeneration, Non-Markovian Systems, Relevance Activation, Aspect Relegation, Cognitive Geometry, RSVP Theory, ATT, CPG Chains, Thermodynamic Semantics.</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="636" data-end="639">
<h2 data-start="641" data-end="692"><strong data-start="644" data-end="690">Part I – The Foundations of Autogeneration</strong></h2>
<p data-start="693" data-end="837"><em data-start="693" data-end="837">Definition of autogeneration, non-Markovian autoregression, trajectory geometry, energy functionals, and information-geometric interpretation.</em></p>
<hr data-start="839" data-end="842">
<h3 data-start="844" data-end="905"><strong data-start="848" data-end="891">Section 1 — Introduction and Motivation</strong> ✅ <em data-start="894" data-end="905">(Written)</em></h3>
<ul data-start="906" data-end="1225">
<li data-start="906" data-end="973">
<p data-start="908" data-end="973">Defines <em data-start="916" data-end="932">autogeneration</em> and <em data-start="937" data-end="953">autoregression</em> as dual concepts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="974" data-end="1038">
<p data-start="976" data-end="1038">Explains the non-Markovian nature of language and cognition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1039" data-end="1132">
<p data-start="1041" data-end="1132">Introduces the “Pregnant Present,” trajectory coherence, and history-dependent inference.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1133" data-end="1225">
<p data-start="1135" data-end="1225">Frames language, cognition, and physics as systems that generate their own continuation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1227" data-end="1305"><strong data-start="1227" data-end="1238">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete (included in the first large LaTeX segment we built).</p>
<hr data-start="1307" data-end="1310">
<h3 data-start="1312" data-end="1377"><strong data-start="1316" data-end="1375">Section 2 — Formal Definition of Autogenerative Systems</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="1378" data-end="1667">
<li data-start="1378" data-end="1481">
<p data-start="1380" data-end="1481">Defines system $\mathcal{S} = (X, \mathcal{T})$ with intrinsic continuation operator $\mathcal{T}$.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1482" data-end="1568">
<p data-start="1484" data-end="1568">Introduces statistical manifolds, Fisher information, and non-Markovian condition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1569" data-end="1667">
<p data-start="1571" data-end="1667">States Conjecture 2.1: <em data-start="1594" data-end="1664">Finite-order Markov models cannot approximate autogenerative systems</em>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1669" data-end="1694"><strong data-start="1669" data-end="1680">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="1696" data-end="1699">
<h3 data-start="1701" data-end="1760"><strong data-start="1705" data-end="1758">Section 3 — Trajectories and the Pregnant Present</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="1761" data-end="1998">
<li data-start="1761" data-end="1849">
<p data-start="1763" data-end="1849">Defines the <em data-start="1775" data-end="1797">trajectory embedding</em> $\phi(x_{1:t})$ and curvature-based continuation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1850" data-end="1916">
<p data-start="1852" data-end="1916">Introduces trajectory energy functional $\mathcal{E}[\gamma]$.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1917" data-end="1998">
<p data-start="1919" data-end="1998">Establishes the principle of smoothness and coherence as energy minimization.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2000" data-end="2025"><strong data-start="2000" data-end="2011">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="2027" data-end="2030">
<h3 data-start="2032" data-end="2100"><strong data-start="2036" data-end="2098">Section 4 — Information Geometry and Statistical Manifolds</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="2101" data-end="2320">
<li data-start="2101" data-end="2154">
<p data-start="2103" data-end="2154">Models token/semantic space as a Fisher manifold.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2155" data-end="2242">
<p data-start="2157" data-end="2242">Shows that autogeneration = geodesic flow on manifold of conditional distributions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2243" data-end="2320">
<p data-start="2245" data-end="2320">Links Barenholtz’s “smooth trajectories” to geodesic energy minimization.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2322" data-end="2347"><strong data-start="2322" data-end="2333">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="2349" data-end="2352">
<h3 data-start="2354" data-end="2418"><strong data-start="2358" data-end="2416">Section 5 — Category-Theoretic and Operator Frameworks</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="2419" data-end="2678">
<li data-start="2419" data-end="2512">
<p data-start="2421" data-end="2512">Introduces language as a monoidal category $\mathcal{L}$ and autoregression as a functor.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2513" data-end="2590">
<p data-start="2515" data-end="2590">Defines natural transformations corresponding to continuation operations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2591" data-end="2678">
<p data-start="2593" data-end="2678">Relates autoregression to Koopman operators and measure-preserving transformations.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2680" data-end="2705"><strong data-start="2680" data-end="2691">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="2707" data-end="2710">
<h3 data-start="2712" data-end="2783"><strong data-start="2716" data-end="2781">Section 6 — Dynamical, Stochastic, and Entropic Formalization</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="2784" data-end="3078">
<li data-start="2784" data-end="2851">
<p data-start="2786" data-end="2851">Defines non-Markovian differential systems and delay equations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2852" data-end="2919">
<p data-start="2854" data-end="2919">Introduces entropy, topological pressure, and ergodic measures.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2920" data-end="2991">
<p data-start="2922" data-end="2991">Connects attention kernels to memory functions and delay equations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2992" data-end="3078">
<p data-start="2994" data-end="3078">Establishes <em data-start="3006" data-end="3022">energy balance</em> between predictive coherence and entropy compression.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3080" data-end="3105"><strong data-start="3080" data-end="3091">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="3107" data-end="3110">
<h3 data-start="3112" data-end="3169"><strong data-start="3116" data-end="3167">Section 7 — Topological Dynamics and Recurrence</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="3170" data-end="3374">
<li data-start="3170" data-end="3229">
<p data-start="3172" data-end="3229">Symbolic dynamics, subshifts, and Conley decomposition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3230" data-end="3306">
<p data-start="3232" data-end="3306">Theorems on recurrence, community persistence, and topological pressure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3307" data-end="3374">
<p data-start="3309" data-end="3374">Introduces predictive free energy as a thermodynamic invariant.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3376" data-end="3428"><strong data-start="3376" data-end="3387">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete (in the most recent LaTeX).</p>
<hr data-start="3430" data-end="3433">
<h3 data-start="3435" data-end="3498"><strong data-start="3439" data-end="3496">Section 8 — Physical and Thermodynamic Interpretation</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="3499" data-end="3822">
<li data-start="3499" data-end="3582">
<p data-start="3501" data-end="3582">Introduces nonlocal action with memory kernel and generalized Noether theorems.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3583" data-end="3657">
<p data-start="3585" data-end="3657">Defines Landauer bound and epistemic work functional $\mathcal{R}[q]$.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3658" data-end="3741">
<p data-start="3660" data-end="3741">Derives fractional (power-law) memory and Wasserstein transport interpretation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3742" data-end="3822">
<p data-start="3744" data-end="3822">Introduces <em data-start="3755" data-end="3778">amplitwistor coupling</em> as physical realization of phase locking.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3824" data-end="3849"><strong data-start="3824" data-end="3835">Status:</strong> ✅ Complete.</p>
<hr data-start="3851" data-end="3854">
<h3 data-start="3856" data-end="3919"><strong data-start="3860" data-end="3917">Section 9 — Cognitive Geometry and Embodied Semantics</strong> ✅</h3>
<ul data-start="3920" data-end="4112">
<li data-start="3920" data-end="3993">
