-end="98">scaffold for Part II – “Advanced Frameworks of Autogeneration.”</strong><br data-start="98" data-end="101">
The goal of this pass is not to fill in every proof, but to give you a <em data-start="172" data-end="203">ready-to-write LaTeX skeleton</em> with:</p>
<ul data-start="211" data-end="527">
<li data-start="211" data-end="249">
<p data-start="213" data-end="249">numbered section headers (§ 13–25)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="250" data-end="307">
<p data-start="252" data-end="307">concise abstracts / guiding theses under each heading</p>
</li>
<li data-start="308" data-end="417">
<p data-start="310" data-end="417">theorem-environment placeholders (Definition, Proposition, Theorem, Corollary) already opened and labeled</p>
</li>
<li data-start="418" data-end="527">
<p data-start="420" data-end="527">short paragraph cues indicating what each section will eventually contain and how it links back to Part I</p>
</li>
</ul>
