" data-end="112">Perfect — same notation (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span></span></span></span>, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span>) and structure: <strong data-start="64" data-end="111">formal first, then cognitive interpretation</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="114" data-end="201">Here’s how I’ll structure <strong data-start="140" data-end="200">Section 14 – Category Theory and ∞-Categorical Coherence</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start="203" data-end="587">
<li data-start="203" data-end="283">
<p data-start="206" data-end="283">Abstract – summarizing the lift from endofunctor to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∞</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>-category</p>
</li>
<li data-start="284" data-end="388">
<p data-start="287" data-end="388">Formal subsection – definitions, propositions, theorems on coherence, adjunctions, higher morphisms</p>
</li>
<li data-start="389" data-end="523">
<p data-start="392" data-end="523">Interpretive subsection – mapping to cognition: attention as 2-morphism, CPG chains as operadic composites, empathy tensors, etc.</p>
</li>
