<h3 data-start="3925" data-end="3941">🔧 <strong data-start="3932" data-end="3941">Notes</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3943" data-end="4495">
<li data-start="3943" data-end="4260">
<p data-start="3945" data-end="4097">The two macros <code data-start="3960" data-end="3977">\ProjectVersion</code> and <code data-start="3982" data-end="3996">\ProjectDate</code> execute small shell commands when running under the Docker container to read from <code data-start="4079" data-end="4094">manifest.yaml</code>.</p>
<ul data-start="4100" data-end="4260">
<li data-start="4100" data-end="4179">
<p data-start="4102" data-end="4179">They will safely default if <code data-start="4130" data-end="4146">--shell-escape</code> is off or the file is missing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4182" data-end="4260">
<p data-start="4184" data-end="4260">This feature works out of the box with your workflow’s Docker environment.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="4262" data-end="4340">
<p data-start="4264" data-end="4340">The <code data-start="4268" data-end="4283">\input{part3}</code> line is commented for now until we scaffold that part.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4342" data-end="4495">
<p data-start="4344" data-end="4495">The <code data-start="4348" data-end="4357">latexmk</code> rule in your Docker build already runs <code data-start="4397" data-end="4412">-shell-escape</code>, so the version/date substitution will work automatically in the Actions pipeline.</p>
</li>
</ul>
