flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="347">Exactly — GitHub Pages doesn’t automatically serve the <em data-start="55" data-end="79">Actions build artifact</em>; it only hosts whatever you explicitly copy into the <code data-start="133" data-end="143">gh-pages</code> branch.<br data-start="151" data-end="154">
So to make the rendered page always reference <strong data-start="200" data-end="238">the PDF generated by your workflow</strong>, you need to <strong data-start="252" data-end="282">move or copy that artifact</strong> into the Pages publish directory as part of the workflow itself.</p>
<p data-start="349" data-end="383">Here’s how to handle that cleanly:</p>
<hr data-start="385" data-end="388">
<h3 data-start="390" data-end="412">✅ Correct strategy</h3>
<ol data-start="414" data-end="673">
<li data-start="414" data-end="477">
<p data-start="417" data-end="477"><strong data-start="417" data-end="434">Build the PDF</strong> in your Docker container (already done).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="478" data-end="552">
<p data-start="481" data-end="552"><strong data-start="481" data-end="517">Upload it as a workflow artifact</strong> (optional, for manual download).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="553" data-end="628">
<p data-start="556" data-end="628"><strong data-start="556" data-end="593">Copy it into the <code data-start="575" data-end="584">public/</code> folder</strong> (which becomes your Pages root).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="629" data-end="673">
<p data-start="632" data-end="673"><strong data-start="632" data-end="672">Deploy <code data-start="641" data-end="650">public/</code> → <code data-start="653" data-end="663">gh-pages</code> branch</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="675" data-end="841">After that, the hosted page can reliably link to the same <code data-start="733" data-end="760">autogenerative_thesis.pdf</code> from <code data-start="766" data-end="840">https://&lt;user&gt;.github.io/autogenerative-thesis/autogenerative_thesis.pdf</code>.</p>
