</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Autogenerative system, axiomatic]
A tuple </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{A}=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{X},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{S},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with:
(i) statistical manifold </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{X}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (Fisher geometry),
(ii) sheaf </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{S}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of continuations with gluing,
(iii) nonlocal flow </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with memory kernel (Volterra/fractional),
(iv) path law </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with polynomial tail dependence,
(v) connection </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on a syntax–semantics bundle.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Equilibrium law]</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{thm:equilibrium-law}
For relevance potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, transjective endofunctor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and epistemic work </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>W</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> R=0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\iff</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2=T </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\iff</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dd</span></span><span> W}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dd</span></span><span> t}=0.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Predictions.}
(1) Polynomial memory law (Thm.~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{thm:poly-tail}).  
(2) Wasserstein smoothness of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
(3) Spectral mass near </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> during automation (Thm.~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{thm:spectral-relegation}).  
(4) Low </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> in high-coherence models.  
