</li>
<li data-start="603" data-end="639">
<p data-start="605" data-end="639">18 → Sheaf Theory and Cohomology</p>
</li>
<li data-start="643" data-end="678">
<p data-start="645" data-end="678">19 → Topos and Contextual Logic</p>
</li>
<li data-start="682" data-end="720">
<p data-start="684" data-end="720">20 → Operads and Generative Syntax</p>
</li>
<li data-start="724" data-end="764">
<p data-start="726" data-end="764">21 → Algebraic Topology of Semantics</p>
</li>
<li data-start="768" data-end="797">
<p data-start="770" data-end="797">22 → Wasserstein Geometry</p>
</li>
<li data-start="801" data-end="834">
<p data-start="803" data-end="834">23 → Spectral Graph Diffusion</p>
</li>
<li data-start="838" data-end="868">
<p data-start="840" data-end="868">24 → Forms and Connections</p>
</li>
<li data-start="872" data-end="920">
<p data-start="874" data-end="920">25 → RSVP Interlude + Transition to Part III</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="922" data-end="1108">
<p data-start="925" data-end="1108"><strong data-start="925" data-end="940">New figures</strong> will be referenced (e.g., <code data-start="967" data-end="990">fig_spectral_flow.pdf</code>, <code data-start="992" data-end="1018">fig_wasserstein_flow.pdf</code>), and I can generate Python scripts to create those later for the <code data-start="1085" data-end="1097" data-is-only-node="">figuregen/</code> directory.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1110" data-end="1275">
<p data-start="1113" data-end="1275">Once Part II is done, I’ll update the ZIP to include the new <code data-start="1174" data-end="1180">.tex</code> content and figure scripts, so your CI will build it into the next PDF artifact automatically.</p>
