<h3 data-start="1363" data-end="1387">📌 How to integrate:</h3>
<ul data-start="1389" data-end="1978">
<li data-start="1389" data-end="1486">
<p data-start="1391" data-end="1486">Use the <code data-start="1399" data-end="1419">kuwada2011coupling</code> entry for your citation corresponding to <code data-start="1461" data-end="1485">\eqref{eq:Lfunctional}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1487" data-end="1563">
<p data-start="1489" data-end="1563">Use the <code data-start="1497" data-end="1519">phillips2021category</code> entry for <code data-start="1530" data-end="1562">Section~\ref{sec:transjective}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1564" data-end="1719">
<p data-start="1566" data-end="1719">In your <code data-start="1574" data-end="1580">.tex</code>, cite with <code data-start="1592" data-end="1624">\parencite{kuwada2011coupling}</code> and <code data-start="1629" data-end="1663">\parencite{phillips2021category}</code> (if using <code data-start="1674" data-end="1684">biblatex</code>) or <code data-start="1689" data-end="1702">\citep{...}</code> if using natbib.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1720" data-end="1978">
<p data-start="1722" data-end="1978">Make sure the label <code data-start="1742" data-end="1758">eq:Lfunctional</code> is defined in your LaTeX (i.e., <code data-start="1791" data-end="1815">\label{eq:Lfunctional}</code> in the equation) and the label <code data-start="1847" data-end="1865">sec:transjective</code> is correctly placed in the section heading (e.g., <code data-start="1916" data-end="1976">\section{Transjective Equivalence}\label{sec:transjective}</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
