<h2 data-start="2766" data-end="2797">🧱 <strong data-start="2772" data-end="2797">Part file conventions</strong></h2>
<p data-start="2799" data-end="2886">Each part file (<code data-start="2815" data-end="2838">part1_foundations.tex</code>, <code data-start="2840" data-end="2871">part2_advanced_frameworks.tex</code>, etc.) should:</p>
<ol data-start="2888" data-end="3152">
<li data-start="2888" data-end="2946">
<p data-start="2891" data-end="2946"><strong data-start="2891" data-end="2898">Not</strong> include <code data-start="2907" data-end="2923">\documentclass</code> or <code data-start="2927" data-end="2945">\begin{document}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2947" data-end="3002">
<p data-start="2950" data-end="3002">Begin directly with <code data-start="2970" data-end="2985">\section{...}</code> or <code data-start="2989" data-end="3001">\part{...}</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3003" data-end="3049">
<p data-start="3006" data-end="3049">Use <code data-start="3010" data-end="3027">\label{sec:...}</code> for cross-references.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3050" data-end="3152">
<p data-start="3053" data-end="3152">Include math, theorems, and figures freely — they inherit all styles and macros from the main file.</p>
</li>
</ol>
