<p data-start="437" data-end="553">That will pop open the folder in Windows Explorer, showing subfolders like <code data-start="512" data-end="517">tex</code>, <code data-start="519" data-end="528">scripts</code>, <code data-start="530" data-end="539">figures</code>, and <code data-start="545" data-end="550">out</code>.</p>
<p data-start="555" data-end="680">If you’re running WSL, it still works — it opens the corresponding Windows path for the current Linux directory. For example:</p>
